  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Several source strings are exhibiting inconsistent usage of the terms \"Audio\" and \"Sounds\" in reference to avatars in Crowdin:\n\n**Avatar sounds**\n\n24731: `Include Avatar Sounds disabled`\n\n24733: `Include Avatar Sounds enabled`\n\n13339: `Audio mutes or unmutes sound effects that emit from a user's avatar for the combined Safety Mode and User Trust Rank.`\n\n13601: `Control the volume of sounds from avatars`\n\n13339: `Audio mutes or unmutes sound effects that emit from a user's avatar for the combined Safety Mode and User Trust Rank.`\n\n**Avatar audio**\n\n24295: `Include Avatar Audio`\n\n14687: `Including Avatar audio.`\n\n23087: `Include avatar audio`\n\n14871: `Include Avatar Audio disabled, click to enable`\n\n14873: `Including Avatar Audio, click to disable`\n\n13595: `Control the master volume for all audio`\n\nShould we stay faithful to the original source strings and use both terms, or?",
